{"title":"2018 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 21","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(CREATIVE_THINKING!!!)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (CREATIVE THINKING!!!)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solutions\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solutions</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>How many positive three-digit integers have a remainder of 2 when divided by 6, a remainder of 5 when divided by 9, and a remainder of 7 when divided by 11?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/a/81ae80de7f9538288c8a0b1d370a58d968bd059d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }1\\qquad\\textbf{(B) }2\\qquad\\textbf{(C) }3\\qquad\\textbf{(D) }4\\qquad \\textbf{(E) }5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"353\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Looking at the values, we notice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/0/dc0d39124d0506809270a4b5a0f3fee4af80cb2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11-7=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"82\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/b/19b3450f6d95edb58cf90cc441daf129b76cd97a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9-5=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"73\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/0/7d026d3bd1e803c6882350c775bcd3cd48b18ed1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6-2=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"73\" height=\"13\" />. This means we are looking for a value that is four less than a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. The least common multiple of these numbers is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/d/f1dbd65c3796c1654c6d5ed4685f68b5c86cc1f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11\\cdot3^{2}\\cdot2=198$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"121\" height=\"15\" />, so the numbers that fulfill this can be written as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/6/af6841a8c320eba6660d11d6521e3cfed0d165ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$198k-4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"70\" height=\"16\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> is a positive integer.  This value is only a three-digit integer when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/0/56018d4175e560429ba86a10b8d6931509ef820f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1, 2, 3, 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"60\" height=\"16\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, which gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/d/f1d725adcb3aa04589a34253cc7ce4728c015209.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$194, 392, 590, 788,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"137\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/2/1e2dd42238eabd8a8c7b790bc001ed5bec08295c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$986$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> respectively. Thus, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> values, so our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b550ea898565bf5504023d5616222edd82b3a267.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E) }5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"54\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let us create the equations: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/1/bf189775893ffd49402662fb9eb391173247c3d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6x+2 = 9y+5 = 11z+7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"208\" height=\"16\" />, and we know <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/1/0d15cfc58e91124c6b83b339c126660c0db7ac85.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100 \\leq 11z+7 &lt;1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"170\" height=\"15\" />, it gives us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/3/aa3b81463b80d31dd0adec3ece62a8962f5350f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9 \\leq z \\leq 90$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"87\" height=\"16\" />, which is the range of the value of z. Because of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/8/638777efab8adb688f6f017c7d6557b5e2dc41d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6x+2=11z+7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"133\" height=\"14\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/8/9f8c1ceef18c067c62742651693f7256ee82abc9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6x=11z+5=6z+5(z+1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"229\" height=\"18\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/6/3f619c5e9e64a41b95ce85c2e910b838f9a7a497.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(z+1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"57\" height=\"20\" /> must be a multiple of 6. Because of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/0/5f07bf41effb66a5a48ba59f5b2e60b4b2bef238.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9y+5=11z+7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"133\" height=\"16\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/7/637c1a6ee65da411cfc1a5b5658fc2f1db53e335.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9y=11z+2=9z+2(z+1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"228\" height=\"18\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/6/3f619c5e9e64a41b95ce85c2e910b838f9a7a497.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(z+1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"57\" height=\"20\" /> must also be a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Hence, the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/6/3f619c5e9e64a41b95ce85c2e910b838f9a7a497.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(z+1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"57\" height=\"20\" /> must be a common multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, which means multiples of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/d/46d0e12bc6adc8d3a321aa91c95c8a1bd542530a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$18 (LCM \\text{ of }\\ 6, 9)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"137\" height=\"20\" />. So, let's say <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/8/e780ab61dd2c013f2ca9844ca68e2e5e19004202.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z+1 = 18p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"92\" height=\"16\" />; then, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/3/6e302662019a91342deacba3ceb592d90e382ddf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9 \\leq z = 18p-1 \\leq 90$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"167\" height=\"16\" />,  so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/a/dda294712d017a23e455f35b50a1dcceb2d469c8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\leq p \\leq 91/18\\ or \\ 1 \\leq p \\leq 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"216\" height=\"18\" />. Thus, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b550ea898565bf5504023d5616222edd82b3a267.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E) }5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"54\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p><p>~LarryFlora\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>By the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Chinese_Remainder_Theorem\" title=\"Chinese Remainder Theorem\">Chinese Remainder Theorem</a>, we have that all solutions are in the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/c/96cc7403b9e0ecf9b0f0d4c32612dd24a9d1b01b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=198k+194$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"123\" height=\"16\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/f/4cf1f08af2da47456891f67ed609c9a9b57184b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k\\in \\mathbb{Z}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"15\" /> Counting the number of values, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/7/3174cd31b5edac0a93789e69a7a8290deb974456.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E) }5}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"61\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~mathboy282\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can use modular arithmetic. Set up the equations: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/4/7f4ee649ae2d9546d7773b5c3ec40fb47d6c61b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\equiv 2 \\mod 6,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"113\" height=\"18\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/7/f57eb9a9c4330fce6070217932227861cbe4007a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\equiv 5 \\mod 9,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"113\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/4/57426ecfd0bec87058fd1994cbe9ae8fb8e335de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\equiv 7 \\mod 11.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"122\" height=\"14\" /> These equations can also be written as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/a/b9a5507f6825d77b15f96e80e5f2cb202c0151cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+4 \\equiv 0 \\mod 6,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"144\" height=\"18\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/7/537b00f32aa97a0dbedeb490172b6588dbf7a350.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+4 \\equiv 0 \\mod 9,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"144\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/2/5828fdeddd27aba7ce340b1c099fabbf8f15aa06.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+4 \\equiv 0 \\mod 11.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"153\" height=\"16\" /> Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/7/ae728897cc815fa29fa3b01affbb9e5592409d2e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" /> is congruent to numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/b/d8bb565b22efa7ff73f411bcea23089fa3840f14.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6, 9,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"30\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/8/f480123fdee29c93742d132dcdab8439a72e45d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"22\" height=\"15\" /> then it must also be congruent to their LCM. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/5/aa594c22585fb292f856c59e9603984e2b7eef0d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+4 \\equiv 0 \\mod 198,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"162\" height=\"18\" /> since 198 is the LCM of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/b/d8bb565b22efa7ff73f411bcea23089fa3840f14.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6, 9,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"30\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/7/4e76ce9da0f428536412a4f539b127c608760686.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11.$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"21\" height=\"12\" /> Since these numbers have to be three digits, they can only be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/d/f1d725adcb3aa04589a34253cc7ce4728c015209.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$194, 392, 590, 788,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"137\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/0/df00785424af145d08c4b94e6c95554fd702cde8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$986.$\" width=\"30\" height=\"12\" /> This gives us the answer of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/7/3174cd31b5edac0a93789e69a7a8290deb974456.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E) }5}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"61\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~ethancui0529\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5\">Solution 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> be the three digit positive integer. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/1/931defaa2bcf79998803243d75ccaae642544c71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N = 6a + 2 = 9b + 5 = 11c + 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"247\" height=\"16\" />. Then, we add four to all sides and write <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/2/3824690570d6b64ceb617e80c0f014ba4bbfc904.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N + 4 = 6(a+1) = 9(b+1) = 11(c+1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"320\" height=\"20\" />. Now, we know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/1/7519c1b823666bca69c4e8020d4eaa71015a8c08.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N + 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"50\" height=\"16\" /> is divisible by 6, 9, and 11. The LCM of 6, 9, and 11 is equal to 198, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/5/4557e91e0dc8ddda5b95795dee6117f0db55a5bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N = 198k - 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"111\" height=\"16\" />. From this, we can figure out that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> can be 5 different three digit numbers -- <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/d/f1d725adcb3aa04589a34253cc7ce4728c015209.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$194, 392, 590, 788,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"137\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/2/1e2dd42238eabd8a8c7b790bc001ed5bec08295c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$986$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/3/a63588d48cc9015ddcfc1560cf86e98b33b51972.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\therefore$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/7/3174cd31b5edac0a93789e69a7a8290deb974456.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E) }5}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"61\" height=\"30\" /> \n</p><p>~DY\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28CREATIVE_THINKING.21.21.21.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(CREATIVE_THINKING!!!)\">Video Solution (CREATIVE THINKING!!!)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (CREATIVE THINKING!!!)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/kb_0r9fEyEI\">https://youtu.be/kb_0r9fEyEI</a>\n</p><p>~Education, the Study of Everything\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by OmegaLearn\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/7an5wU9Q5hk?t=939\">https://youtu.be/7an5wU9Q5hk?t=939</a> \n</p><p>~ pi_is_3.14\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solutions\">Video Solutions</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solutions\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/CPQpkpnEuIc\">https://youtu.be/CPQpkpnEuIc</a> \n</p><p>~ Happytwin\n</p><p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/hoCdk8AC-0c\">https://youtu.be/hoCdk8AC-0c</a>\n</p><p>~savannahsolver\n</p><p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=PjYwbGm_2aM\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=PjYwbGm_2aM</a>   ~David\n</p><p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/7xlBdxcsP3I?si=lfZZBB7i_6tOlKr-\">https://youtu.be/7xlBdxcsP3I?si=lfZZBB7i_6tOlKr-</a>\n</p><p>Pi Academy (Fast and Easy)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_8\" title=\"2018 AMC 8\">2018 AMC 8</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_8_Problems\" title=\"2018 AMC 8 Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_8_Answer_Key\" title=\"2018 AMC 8 Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=42&amp;year=2018\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2018 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 20\">Problem 20</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?